messages:
maria: FYI CI is failing on the chart lint for inference-nodepool after the values.schema addition. ct job shows helm lint/template errors on the GPU helpers.

maria: Error from CI: ```
Error: template: inference-nodepool/templates/deployment.yaml:45:12: executing "inference-nodepool/templates/deployment.yaml" at <.Values.node.gpu.count>: nil pointer evaluating interface {}.
helm lint exited with 1
```

devon: I think this is because the schema now requires `node.gpu` in some permutations and our helper uses `required` directly which makes `helm template` blow up during lint. Lint runs without the secrets/overrides we use in prod.

samir: yup — we hit that before. Two options: (1) loosen the values.schema so `node.gpu` can be null/absent (preferred), or (2) make the helper resilient using `hasKey`/`default` and only call `required` at runtime when deploying with validated inputs.

jen: CI runs are `ct --lint` + `helm template --debug`. In our pipeline we run `helm template` without `--set` for cluster-specific keys, so templates must be defensive. Also worth adding a tiny ct test values file for the non-GPU path so we don't regress.

ops-bot: [ci/inference-nodepool-lint] Job failed: https://ci.redwood.example/jobs/2034 — failing step: helm-lint (exit 1) :warning:

maria: Proposed quick fix I tested locally: change helper from: ```
{{- define "inference.node.gpuCount" -}}
{{- required "node.gpu.count is required" .Values.node.gpu.count -}}
{{- end -}}
```
to: ```
{{- define "inference.node.gpuCount" -}}
{{- if hasKey .Values "node" -}}
  {{- if hasKey .Values.node "gpu" -}}
    {{- default 0 .Values.node.gpu.count | int -}}
  {{- else -}}
    0
  {{- end -}}
{{- else -}}
  0
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
```
This avoids nil deref in `helm template` and keeps runtime behavior sane (we default to 0 GPUs).

devon: That looks good. Also for the schema I'd allow both `nvidia.com/gpu` and `accelerator` node labels in the docs — some regions (or private infra) use a different label name. Maybe update values.schema to accept a `node.selector` map with additionalProperties: true, or include a small `oneOf` so both shapes validate.

samir: small caution: using `default 0` hides cases where someone truly forgot to set GPU for a GPU-only deploy. We should keep a runtime validation step in the operator/k8s job that runs during dedicated provisioning (not in helm lint). E.g., a preflight job that checks `if .Values.node.gpu.required == true and count == 0 then fail` — that won't run during `helm template` though.

jen: I'll add a ct test: `tests/values-nogpu.yaml` and `tests/values-withgpu.yaml` to the chart so ct covers both code paths. Also adding a small README note about region label differences so infra knows to set the right override.

maria: Good plan. I'll open the PR with: (1) helper change, (2) loosened values.schema allowing `node.gpu` to be nullable and `node.selector` as map<string, string>, (3) two ct test values files, (4) README note. Will run ct locally and push. CC @jen to review tests.

devon: +1 please also add a line in CHANGELOG about the schema relaxation and the risk note Samir mentioned.

maria: Will do. PR will be up in ~30m.

jen: Thanks — lemme know when CI passes and I'll merge. :thumbsup:
